<p>Hi {{{Recovery__c.Contact_First_Name__c}}},&nbsp;</p>

<p>We want to apologise for any inconvenience caused. Our goal is to make sure you receive your reimbursement quickly and seamlessly.</p>

<p><strong>Your reimbursement amount</strong></p>

<p>You will receive a reimbursement of <strong>{{{Recovery__c.Value__c}}}</strong>.</p>

<p>Payments made to bank accounts outside of Australia will be converted into the equivalent local currency at the time of payment.</p>

<p><strong>How to organise your reimbursement</strong><br />
<br />
To process your reimbursement, you will need to provide us with your bank account details using our secure case portal. Visit <a href="https://www.qantas.com/au/en/support/contact-us/customer-care-feedback-form/update-customer-care-case.html">https://www.qantas.com/au/en/support/contact-us/customer-care-feedback-form/update-customer-care-case.html</a> &nbsp;to commence your reimbursement.&nbsp;<br />
<br />
All customers will receive email notifications about the progress of the claim. If you are a Qantas Frequent Flyer member, you can conveniently track your reimbursement via the request tracker in the Qantas app via ‘Track my cases’ in Help and Support.</p>

<p><strong>Need Help?</strong></p>

<p>Call us on 13 13 13 (in Australia) or your local <a href="https://www.qantas.com/au/en/support/contact-us.html" target="_blank">Qantas Office</a> for assistance.</p>

<p><strong>If you’re suspicious:</strong></p>

<p>Not sure something is genuine? Remember, Qantas will never ask you to <u>email</u> your bank account details,&nbsp;credit card, PIN, or passwords.<br />
For more advice and warnings on scams please visit the Qantas scam assistance page - <a href="https://www.qantas.com/au/en/support/contact-us/scam-assistance.html" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">https://www.qantas.com/au/en/support/contact-us/scam-assistance.html</a></p>
